### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 09 — AUTONOMOUS CRON SCHEDULER
###
### ArcClaw supports scheduling future agent tasks using the cron
### scheduler. Agents schedule tasks via ScheduleTaskTool and list/
### manage them via ManageScheduleTool or zero-token reflexes.
###
### Only coordinator and synthesizer roles can schedule tasks
### (they are the only ones with scheduletask in their tool schema).
###
### How it works end-to-end:
###   1. User instructs coordinator to schedule a task
###   2. Agent invokes ScheduleTaskTool with:
###        cronExpression (5-field UNIX), goal, timezone, runOnce
###   3. ScheduleTaskTool validates expr via cron-utils, writes AgentCronEntity
###   4. AgentCronScheduler polls SQLite every 30 seconds
###   5. On fire: CronJobRunner executes agent loop (maxIterations=2)
###   6. CronResultHandler fires CDI AgentJobCompleted event
###
### Safeguards built into ScheduleTaskTool:
###   - Fork-bomb guard: goal prefixed with CRON:; nested CRON: rejected
###   - Naked-pronoun guard: vague goals ("it", "this", "that") rejected
###   - runOnce=true → job row deleted after first execution
###
### Management via reflexes (zero-token):
###   /crons       → list all jobs for the current user
###   /cron        → alias
###   /list crons  → alias
###   deletecron <id> → delete job by ID
###
### Management via ManageScheduleTool (LLM-invoked):
###   action=list   → same as /crons reflex
###   action=delete, cronId=<id> → same as deletecron reflex
###
### IMPORTANT: These tests require GROQ_API_KEY and GITHUB_TOKEN to be set.
### The agent must successfully call ScheduleTaskTool for cron rows to appear.
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
@validKey = Fxa8CCQGpjHr7DS3eiSTlb3W0RKzImwHXPkNbq9S98c=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SETUP: Session for cron scheduling tests
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-0] Create session for cron tests
# @name cronSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SCHEDULE A RECURRING TASK
# The coordinator invokes ScheduleTaskTool internally.
# Audit event CRONCREATED is written when the tool succeeds.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-1] Schedule a task that fires every minute (for testing)
# The agent parses "every minute" and converts to cron expression: "* * * * *"
# Expect 200: agent confirms the schedule was created with a cron ID
# Check audit log for: eventType=CRONCREATED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a task to run every minute that answers: What is the current JVM uptime in seconds?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

### [CRON-2] Schedule a one-shot task (runOnce=true)
# runOnce=true → row is deleted after first fire
# The agent sets runOnce flag in the ScheduleTaskTool invocation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a one-time task to run in 2 minutes from now that prints: ArcClaw cron job executed successfully.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

### [CRON-3] Schedule task with a specific timezone
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a task to run every day at 9 AM IST (Asia/Kolkata timezone) that summarizes: Daily health check complete.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LIST SCHEDULED TASKS
# Three equivalent zero-token reflex paths — all query the same table
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-4] /crons — list via reflex (no LLM call)
# Expect: formatted list of all cron jobs for this user, including IDs
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [CRON-5] /list crons — natural language alias
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/list crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [CRON-6] List via ManageScheduleTool (agent-invoked)
# This uses the LLM to invoke ManageScheduleTool with action=list
# Coordinator has manageschedule in its tool schema
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Using the manage schedule tool, list all my scheduled tasks.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

### This always returns 200 if the key is valid — good for rate limit testing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}



### [SESSION-3] Check status after sync run
# Expect 200: {"sessionId":"...","status":"COMPLETED","steps":[...],"failReason":null}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}


###

### [CRON-7] List the public repositories of GitHub user rsrini7 using the github tool.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "schedule to List the public repositories of GitHub user rsrini7 using the github tool after 1 minute",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DELETE SCHEDULED TASKS
# Note: copy an actual cron ID from the /crons response above
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-7] deletecron via reflex — replace CRON_ID with actual value from CRON-4
# DeleteCronReflex: matches "deletecron <id>" prefix
# Expect: "✅ Cron job <id> deleted." or "❌ Cron job not found."
# Audit event: CRONDELETED
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "deletecron 3243e38f-1bf3-4df5-8445-a3c1c7186c61",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [CRON-8] Delete via ManageScheduleTool (agent-invoked)
# Coordinator invokes ManageScheduleTool with action=delete, cronId=<id>
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Using the manage schedule tool, delete cron job with ID REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_CRON_ID.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [CRON-9] Delete non-existent cron ID → expect "not found" message
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "deletecron 00000000-dead-beef-0000-000000000000",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SAFEGUARD TESTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-10] Naked-pronoun guard — vague goal should be rejected by ScheduleTaskTool
# ScheduleTaskTool rejects goals containing "it", "this", "that", "the result"
# without sufficient specificity. Expect: agent returns error asking to restate goal.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a task to run every hour to do it again.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 3
}

###

### [CRON-11] Coder role cannot schedule — schema filter prevents it
# Brahma has no scheduletask tool in its schema → LLM cannot invoke it
# Expect: agent explains it cannot schedule tasks
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a task to run every morning at 8 AM that prints hello.",
    "agentRole": "coder",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# WAIT & OBSERVE CRON EXECUTION
# AgentCronScheduler polls every 30 seconds.
# After scheduling CRON-1 (every minute), wait ~90 seconds then:
#   1. Check audit for CRONFIRED event
#   2. Check audit for CRONFAILED (if an error occurred)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-12] Check audit for CRONFIRED event (run after ~90 seconds)
# Expect: eventType=CRONFIRED in the audit list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit/session/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [CRON-13] List crons after execution — runOnce job should be gone
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/crons",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SYNTHESIZER — also has cron scheduling capability
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [CRON-14] Synthesizer (Dattatreya) can also schedule tasks
# @name synthCronSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{synthCronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Schedule a one-time task to run in 1 minute that performs a cross-domain summary: what are the key JVM metrics an AI agent kernel should monitor?",
    "agentRole": "synthesizer",
    "maxIterations": 5
}

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{synthCronSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/crons",
    "agentRole": "synthesizer",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLEANUP
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{cronSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{synthCronSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-ArcClaw-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###
